## A stand-in language server

The bridge is tested against a language server small enough to read. `standInServer` writes one to a scratch folder as an executable script with no dependencies. It frames LSP messages on its standard streams by hand, answers `initialize`, a hover and a pulled diagnostic, and writes one line to its log for every message it receives, so a case can read back exactly what the bridge sent and in what order. It writes `started` and its process id to the log when it starts, so a case can count how many processes ran and check whether one still runs.

A few file names make it misbehave, the way a real server might on some input. Any message about a file whose name holds `crash`, other than closing it, makes it exit at once, so a file opened at start ends the server as soon as it starts. A hover on a file whose name holds `boom` makes it exit then, after it has run for a while. A hover on a file whose name holds `garble` makes it answer with a message that is not JSON, and keep running. A hover on a file whose name holds `refuse` makes it answer with an error, `no project here`, and keep running, the way a real server refuses a question it cannot answer.

The stand-in is written with plain loops and string handling. It is a fixture that stands in for a foreign program, not code of Loom's, and it must run alone, with nothing to import.

=>

import { chmodSync, mkdtempSync, readFileSync, realpathSync, writeFileSync } from 'node:fs'
import { tmpdir } from 'node:os'
import { join } from 'node:path'

export interface StandIn {
  readonly command: string
  readonly log: string
  readonly folder: string
  readonly lines: () => ReadonlyArray<string>
}

const standInSource = (log: string): string => `#!/usr/bin/env bun
const { appendFileSync } = require('node:fs')
const log = (line) => appendFileSync(${JSON.stringify(log)}, line + '\\n')
log('started ' + process.pid)
let buffer = Buffer.alloc(0)
const write = (message) => {
  const body = JSON.stringify({ jsonrpc: '2.0', ...message })
  process.stdout.write('Content-Length: ' + Buffer.byteLength(body) + '\\r\\n\\r\\n' + body)
}
const reply = (id, result) => write({ id, result })
const handle = (message) => {
  const uri = message.params?.textDocument?.uri ?? ''
  const version = message.params?.textDocument?.version
  log(message.method + (uri ? ' ' + uri.split('/').pop() : '') + (version ? ' v' + version : ''))
  if (uri.includes('crash') && message.method !== 'textDocument/didClose') process.exit(1)
  if (uri.includes('boom') && message.method === 'textDocument/hover') process.exit(1)
  if (uri.includes('garble') && message.method === 'textDocument/hover') {
    return process.stdout.write('Content-Length: 9\\r\\n\\r\\nnot json!')
  }
  if (message.id === undefined) return
  if (uri.includes('refuse') && message.method === 'textDocument/hover') {
    return write({ id: message.id, error: { code: -32803, message: 'no project here' } })
  }
  if (message.method === 'initialize') return reply(message.id, { capabilities: {} })
  if (message.method === 'textDocument/hover') return reply(message.id, { contents: 'stand-in' })
  if (message.method === 'textDocument/diagnostic') return reply(message.id, { kind: 'full', items: [] })
  return reply(message.id, null)
}
process.stdin.on('data', (chunk) => {
  buffer = Buffer.concat([buffer, chunk])
  for (;;) {
    const end = buffer.indexOf('\\r\\n\\r\\n')
    if (end < 0) return
    const length = Number(/Content-Length: (\\d+)/i.exec(buffer.subarray(0, end).toString())[1])
    if (buffer.length < end + 4 + length) return
    const body = buffer.subarray(end + 4, end + 4 + length).toString()
    buffer = buffer.subarray(end + 4 + length)
    handle(JSON.parse(body))
  }
})
`

export const standInServer = (): StandIn => {
  const folder = realpathSync(mkdtempSync(join(tmpdir(), 'loom-stand-in-')))
  const command = join(folder, 'stand-in-server')
  const log = join(folder, 'log')
  writeFileSync(log, '')
  writeFileSync(command, standInSource(log))
  chmodSync(command, 0o755)
  return {
    command,
    log,
    folder,
    lines: () => readFileSync(log, 'utf8').split('\n').filter((line) => line !== ''),
  }
}

export const settled = (ms = 300): Promise<void> => new Promise((resolve) => setTimeout(resolve, ms))

export const startedIn = (lines: ReadonlyArray<string>): ReadonlyArray<number> =>
  lines.filter((line) => line.startsWith('started ')).map((line) => Number(line.split(' ')[1]))

export const running = (pid: number): boolean => {
  try {
    process.kill(pid, 0)
    return true
  } catch {
    return false
  }
}

## The stand-in module {Tangle}[test/StandInServer.ts]

=>

::[A stand-in language server]

## Testing the bridge

These cases drive the bridge against the stand-in server, and against commands that cannot start.

The first case checks what `keepOpen` sends and in what order. It opens `a.ts`, then changes it and opens `b.ts`, then leaves only `b.ts`. Within a call the bridge opens new files before it changes old ones, so the server receives `a.ts` at version one, `b.ts` at version one, `a.ts` at version two, and a close for `a.ts`. A request sent last reaches the server after all of them.

The next cases check that a server which cannot start never takes the host down. A command that does not exist, a file that cannot be executed, a folder that does not exist, and a server that exits as soon as it starts each leave the bridge not alive, and a request fails with `LanguageServerFailed` instead of crashing the test process. A server that answers with a message that is not JSON is stopped, and its process no longer runs.

Two cases check what a failed request says. A server that answers a hover with an error keeps running, and the failure repeats the server's words. A server that crashes while a hover waits is reported as not running, never as having answered, although `vscode-jsonrpc` fails the waiting request with an error of its own. `dispose` stops the process, and a second call does nothing.

The last case runs the bridge under Node, the runtime the VS Code extension and the npm command use. It starts Node on a small script that imports the bridge's own source, which Node runs by stripping its types, and has the bridge ask the stand-in for a hover. The case passes only if the hover comes back, so a module name Node cannot resolve fails it. A machine without Node skips it.

=>

import { describe, expect, it } from 'bun:test'
import { spawnSync } from 'node:child_process'
import { join } from 'node:path'
import { writeFileSync } from 'node:fs'
import { LanguageServerFailed, spawnLanguageServer } from '../src/LanguageServerProcess'
import { running, settled, standInServer, startedIn } from './StandInServer'

describe('LanguageServerProcess keeps files open and sends requests in order', () => {
  it('opens, changes and closes files, and sends a request after them', async () => {
    const stand = standInServer()
    const server = spawnLanguageServer(stand.command, [], stand.folder, 'typescript', {})
    server.keepOpen([{ path: join(stand.folder, 'a.ts'), text: 'one' }])
    server.keepOpen([
      { path: join(stand.folder, 'a.ts'), text: 'two' },
      { path: join(stand.folder, 'b.ts'), text: 'three' },
    ])
    server.keepOpen([{ path: join(stand.folder, 'b.ts'), text: 'three' }])
    const hover = await server.request<{ readonly contents: string }>('textDocument/hover', {
      textDocument: { uri: `file://${join(stand.folder, 'b.ts')}` },
      position: { line: 0, character: 0 },
    })
    expect(hover.contents).toBe('stand-in')
    expect(stand.lines().slice(1)).toEqual([
      'initialize',
      'initialized',
      'textDocument/didOpen a.ts v1',
      'textDocument/didOpen b.ts v1',
      'textDocument/didChange a.ts v2',
      'textDocument/didClose a.ts',
      'textDocument/hover b.ts',
    ])
    server.dispose()
  })
})

describe('LanguageServerProcess never takes the host down when a server cannot start', () => {
  const unstartable = async (command: string, folder: string) => {
    const server = spawnLanguageServer(command, [], folder, 'typescript', {})
    server.keepOpen([{ path: join(folder, 'a.ts'), text: 'one' }])
    const failure = await server.request('textDocument/hover', {}).then(
      () => undefined,
      (error: unknown) => error,
    )
    await settled()
    return { failure, alive: server.alive() }
  }

  it('reports a command that does not exist', async () => {
    const stand = standInServer()
    const { failure, alive } = await unstartable(join(stand.folder, 'missing'), stand.folder)
    expect(failure).toBeInstanceOf(LanguageServerFailed)
    expect(alive).toBe(false)
  })

  it('reports a file that cannot be executed', async () => {
    const stand = standInServer()
    const plain = join(stand.folder, 'plain')
    writeFileSync(plain, 'not a program')
    const { failure, alive } = await unstartable(plain, stand.folder)
    expect(failure).toBeInstanceOf(LanguageServerFailed)
    expect(alive).toBe(false)
  })

  it('reports a folder that does not exist', async () => {
    const stand = standInServer()
    const { failure, alive } = await unstartable(stand.command, join(stand.folder, 'gone'))
    expect(failure).toBeInstanceOf(LanguageServerFailed)
    expect(alive).toBe(false)
  })

  it('reports a server that exits as soon as it starts', async () => {
    const stand = standInServer()
    const quitter = join(stand.folder, 'quitter')
    writeFileSync(quitter, '#!/bin/sh\nexit 3\n', { mode: 0o755 })
    const { failure, alive } = await unstartable(quitter, stand.folder)
    expect(failure).toBeInstanceOf(LanguageServerFailed)
    expect(alive).toBe(false)
  })

  it('stops a server that answers with a message it cannot read', async () => {
    const stand = standInServer()
    const server = spawnLanguageServer(stand.command, [], stand.folder, 'typescript', {})
    const failure = await server
      .request('textDocument/hover', { textDocument: { uri: `file://${join(stand.folder, 'garble.ts')}` } })
      .then(
        () => undefined,
        (error: unknown) => error,
      )
    await settled()
    expect(failure).toBeInstanceOf(LanguageServerFailed)
    expect(server.alive()).toBe(false)
    expect(startedIn(stand.lines()).every((pid) => !running(pid))).toBe(true)
  })
})

describe('LanguageServerProcess tells an error answer from a crash', () => {
  const hoverFailure = async (file: string) => {
    const stand = standInServer()
    const server = spawnLanguageServer(stand.command, [], stand.folder, 'typescript', {})
    const failure = await server
      .request('textDocument/hover', { textDocument: { uri: `file://${join(stand.folder, file)}` } })
      .then(
        () => undefined,
        (error: unknown) => error as LanguageServerFailed,
      )
    await settled()
    const alive = server.alive()
    server.dispose()
    return { failure, alive }
  }

  it('repeats the words of a server that answered with an error', async () => {
    const { failure, alive } = await hoverFailure('refuse.ts')
    expect(failure?.message).toContain('answered: no project here')
    expect(alive).toBe(true)
  })

  it('reports a server that crashed mid-request as not running', async () => {
    const { failure, alive } = await hoverFailure('boom.ts')
    expect(failure?.message).toContain('is not running')
    expect(failure?.message).not.toContain('answered')
    expect(alive).toBe(false)
  })
})

describe('LanguageServerProcess shuts a server down once', () => {
  it('stops the process, and a second dispose does nothing', async () => {
    const stand = standInServer()
    const server = spawnLanguageServer(stand.command, [], stand.folder, 'typescript', {})
    await server.request('textDocument/hover', {})
    server.dispose()
    server.dispose()
    await settled()
    expect(server.alive()).toBe(false)
    expect(stand.lines().filter((line) => line === 'shutdown')).toEqual(['shutdown'])
  })
})

describe('LanguageServerProcess runs under Node', () => {
  const node = spawnSync('node', ['--version']).status === 0

  it.skipIf(!node)('starts a server and gets an answer when Node runs it', () => {
    const stand = standInServer()
    const script = join(stand.folder, 'under-node.ts')
    const bridge = join(import.meta.dir, '..', 'src', 'LanguageServerProcess.ts')
    writeFileSync(
      script,
      `import { spawnLanguageServer } from ${JSON.stringify(bridge)}\n` +
        `const server = spawnLanguageServer(${JSON.stringify(stand.command)}, [], ${JSON.stringify(stand.folder)}, 'typescript', {})\n` +
        `server.request('textDocument/hover', {}).then(\n` +
        `  (hover) => { console.log(JSON.stringify(hover)); server.dispose() },\n` +
        `  (error) => { console.log('failed: ' + error.message); server.dispose() },\n` +
        `)\n`,
    )
    const run = spawnSync('node', [script], { cwd: join(import.meta.dir, '..'), encoding: 'utf8', timeout: 20_000 })
    expect(run.stdout.trim()).toBe(JSON.stringify({ contents: 'stand-in' }))
  })
})

